 inside the united states  capital i was we could walk through how  it feels to be hunted you walk through  rolling your sleeves up taking your tie  off and literally asking yourself what  weapon can i find to defend myself until  i die yeah you talked about it i had a  pain in my hand absolutely talked about  actually calming everybody down and say  look everybody let's let's just take a  second but i want to go back to donald  trump's role in it for just a second he  has taken no uh responsibility for it  and january 6 you heard from rioters who  said look we went because he asked us to  we were there because he called us there  doesn't the president have don't his  words have power and shouldn't he be  more careful with his words yes he was  encouraging people that he knew were  armed well i i don't know that anyone  knows  that the crowd was armed when they uh  called to come to the capitol  was was put out there number one number  two i would say this though  every person  has the responsibility  of taking fully the decisions that they  make and be responsible for those  decisions  i think giving that to anybody other  than the individual  is giving the individual a pass but  president have responsibility to senator  of course of course of course some would  say the most responsibility i would say  that we all have the most responsibility  for our own words this is easy uh for us  to put the blame on someone else right  but  as the guy that felt hunted in the  moment and  watching my watching my senate  colleagues  look for a route to escape one of the  things you'll see in the book is how  important it is in the middle of a  chaotic situation to find peace clarity  and then be decisive in going back out  that same way you sounded terrifying can  i vision can i talk about chapter five  in the book because the headline is tim  scott for president oh  oh he's he's getting ready to tell us  something tim scott for president the  beginning of chapter five right  um